-- the growth iterated a given number of times, keeping the atoms distinct: with the number of atoms as
-- the bound this reaches the orbit under the group the generators generate, since each step that adds
-- nothing leaves the list unchanged. Generators suffice, which is what makes a real molecule tractable:
-- the group of valine's bond graph has 36 elements and four generators.
orbit-iter : (M : Mol) → (mol-atoms M → mol-atoms M → Bool) → List (Auto M) → Nat → List (mol-atoms M) → List (mol-atoms M)
orbit-iter M eq gens n ys = case n of
  zero → ys
  suc k → orbit-iter M eq gens k (nub-by (mol-atoms M) eq (chem-append (mol-atoms M) ys (orbit-step M gens ys)))
